==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Aoi Hayakawa CC''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Baseball Mask α''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
As an [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] with laughable range, she's pretty situational. Since her main point is to deal massive rapid damage against any Alien, she's best used against enemies like [[LeMurr]] or [[Kroxo|peons]] with that trait. However, if obtained early on, her damage is sufficient enough to help a player charge right through stages easily, and helps quite a bit in [[Into the Future|Into The Future]]'s earlier chapters. However, when she obtains her True Form, her power really shines through. In exchange for a lengthened attack rate, her range becomes useful and the radius that the attack hits in becomes significantly larger.

Treat her as though she was the Super Rare equivalent of [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]]. While she has more health and damage (also range in True Form), Chill Cat has a significant shorter recharge time and about a second less time between its attacks, more so if Aoi is in her true form, where her time between attacks lengthens. Since Chill is part of every gacha, Chill Cat can get much higher stats due to plus levels.

==='''True Form'''===
Baseball Mask α, if positioned correctly, can outrange annoying alien backliners like [[Ursamajor]] or [[Maawth]], due to her LD reaching up to 400 (although she can't outrange enemies with higher range over 400, like [[Elder Sloth]] or [[Alpacky]]).

Due to her low number of knockbacks, she has difficulty against enemies entering her blindspot, just like all long distance units.

Unfortunately, using traditional rangers are easier to handle. Her extremely long recharge also affects comparability to attackers like [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] and [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Lizard Cat]]. Furthermore, her greater than average movement speed may cause her to rush into enemies, who will then push into her blindspot.

